# General
.DS_Store
# `.env` ALONE WAS NOT ENOUGH, AND THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC (2026-09-02).
#
# `infrastructure/local/env-from-prod.sh` keeps the previous file as `infrastructure/.env.bak` - it
# has to, because that is where it reads the local auth secrets back from so a re-run does not
# desynchronise the running containers. `.env` did not match `.env.bak`, so `git add -A` staged
# 7930 bytes of PRODUCTION credentials, and it was caught in the commit rather than on the remote.
#
# `frontend/.gitignore` already had the right rule (`.env.*` with `!.env.example`); this file is now
# aligned with it. The negation matters: three `.env.example` templates are tracked on purpose.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock
.canari_pids

