# Figma
Figma/


# Generated sources - built, never committed.
#
# A generated file in git is a copy of the truth, and a copy goes stale in silence: the
# committed WASM was a crypto fix behind the sources for weeks, and only the pipelines that
# happened to rebuild it shipped the fix. Every pipeline that ships a client now builds it
# (.github/actions/build-mls-wasm), and `npm run generate` does the same on a dev machine.
# `src/lib/paraglide/` already worked this way and never drifted.
frontend/src/lib/wasm/
frontend/src/lib/proto/canari.js
frontend/src/lib/proto/canari.d.ts

# Application specific
apps/user-service/bin/

# Test coverage
*.lcov
lcov-report/
.nyc_output/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
*.cache

*.lock
# A lockfile is committed when the package it locks is itself built into a SHIPPED
# artefact, so that CI, Docker and a developer machine all resolve the exact same
# dependency tree instead of floating ranges. A crate that only ever gets consumed
# as a dependency (mls-core) resolves inside its consumer's lock and
# keeps none of its own - hence no exception for those.
# These negations must stay AFTER the `*.lock` above: the last matching pattern wins.
!frontend/bun.lock
!apps/core-service/bun.lock
!apps/social-service/bun.lock
!apps/media-service/bun.lock
!apps/chat-delivery-service/bun.lock
!frontend/src-tauri/Cargo.lock
!frontend/mls-wasm/Cargo.lock
!apps/*/Cargo.lock

# Apple artefacts
._*
*.xcuserdatad

# Secrets / signing keys - never commit (Firebase client configs are injected by
# CI, the APNs .p8 auth key lives only in the Firebase console).
*.p8
GoogleService-Info.plist
google-services.json

# Aider
.aider*

# Python (test_adb.py tooling)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# TLS material for the LOCAL estate, minted by make-local-cert.sh. The CA private key is a
# development secret and the leaf is machine-specific; both are regenerable in one command, so
# neither belongs in a PUBLIC repository.
infrastructure/local/certs/

# The debug-only Android trust override, written by tools/cross-client-harness/a1apk.mjs. It holds a
# COPY of the local development CA, which is a credential and is gitignored at its source - and the
# whole directory is generated, per workstation, from a certificate that `--force` can replace.
frontend/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/debug/
